rease going away from the trunk, on both the right and the left. The first branch is always on the right."},{"type":"text","tex":"This tree uses the integers 1 to 6. It has 2 branches with 2 leaves on each branch."},{"type":"figure","id":"0607_2024MJ_52_tA_diagram1"},{"type":"text","tex":"This tree uses the integers 1 to 12. It has 4 branches with 2 leaves on each branch. The leaves furthest from the trunk are the outer leaves."},{"type":"figure","id":"0607_2024MJ_52_tA_diagram2"},{"type":"text","tex":"A is the sum of the left outer leaves."},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(B\\) is the sum of the right outer leaves."},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(T\\) is the sum of the integers in the trunk."},{"type":"text","tex":"Example"},{"type":"text","tex":"For the tree with 4 branches,"},{"type":"text","tex":"A \\(= 6+12 = 18\\)"},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(B = 3+9 = 12\\)"},{"type":"text","tex":"\\(T = 1+4+7+10 = 22\\) ."},{"type":"text","tex":"In Questions 1 to 5, the number of branches, \\(n\\) , is always even."}],"tex_check":"ok"}]}